※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ **A generic function takes arguments by name and has defaults**, as any other
※ function does: what each argument settles about the types is read in the
※ order the parameters are written, whatever order the call writes them in, and
※ a default is read where the definition is.

fn picked(one: T', other: T', first: bool ← true) → T':
    if first: one else: other

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if picked(3u8, 2u8) ≠ 3u8:
        return 1u6
    if picked(3u8, .first ← false, .other ← 4u8) ≠ 4u8:
        return 2u6
    if picked(2i16, 5i16, false) ≠ 5i16:
        return 3u6
    0u6
